data.content:
## What Breaks in .NET 11

In EF Core 11 (Cosmos provider), the **sync-over-async opt-in is removed entirely**. The synchronous APIs now throw `InvalidOperationException` — there's no configuration to re-enable them.

**All four methods break:**

| Method | Sync call that throws | Async replacement |
|--------|----------------------|-------------------|
| `GetAll()` | `ToList()` | `await ToListAsync()` |
| `GetById()` | `First(...)` | `await FirstAsync(...)` |
| `GetCount()` | `Count()` | `await CountAsync()` |
| `Save()` | `SaveChanges()` | `await SaveChangesAsync()` |

## The Fix

Convert to async throughout:

```csharp
public class ProductRepository
{
    private readonly CosmosDbContext _context;

    public async Task<List<Product>> GetAllAsync()
    {
        return await _context.Products.ToListAsync();
    }

    public async Task<Product> GetByIdAsync(int id)
    {
        return await _context.Products.FirstAsync(p => p.Id == id);
    }

    public async Task<int> GetCountAsync()
    {
        return await _context.Products.CountAsync();
    }

    public async Task SaveAsync(Product product)
    {
        _context.Products.Add(product);
        await _context.SaveChangesAsync();
    }
}
```

**Why the change:** The Cosmos DB SDK is inherently async. The sync wrappers used `.GetAwaiter().GetResult()`, risking deadlocks and thread-pool starvation. EF Core 10 warned and offered an opt-in; EF Core 11 removes the path entirely.

You'll also need to propagate `async/await` up to your controllers/handlers (async all the way).
